current settings of these parameters and to dump out  the  values
of  the  card’s statistics counters.  Most of the parameters that
can be changed relate to the 802.11  protocol  which  the  imple‐
ments.   This  includes  the station name, whether the station is
operating in ad‐hoc (point to point) or BSS (service  set)  mode,
and  the network name of a service set to join (IBSS) if BSS mode
is enabled.  The argument given to should be the  logical  inter‐
face  name  associated  with  the  device (e.g., wi0, wi1, etc.).
